{"id": "EUVD-2026-105100", "enisaUuid": "d51f3e66-ac82-3834-be60-dd48168f70fd", "description": "Missing authorisation checks in chttpd in Apache CouchDB 3.5.2 and below on all platforms allows any request to read the full contents of a prefixed _user or _replicator database via an unauthorised API endpoint.\n\n\nThe use of prefixed system databases is very rare.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 3.5.3, which fixes this issue.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T18:10:09", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:H/SI:H/SA:N/E:U/S:N/AU:Y/R:U/V:C/RE:M/U:Amber", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/pj83174r8f8f64odf47fwhozbfjtot0f", "https://lists.apache.org/thread/vng8vqjwgy1qlrv14wzrgs7pv4gj7gwr"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90800", "GHSA-49pc-3x56-3wp6"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.63, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a9ce0dd0-ca55-3705-973a-9dfd4418cf3a", "product": {"name": "Apache CouchDB", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.5.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6f5109d9-0047-37cf-8d67-56d692050140", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}